    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with significant upside, spearheaded by the elite output of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) and **Yordan Alvarez** (81.62). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play; he benefits from a highly favorable matchup against Houck, where his elite sprint speed is amplified by the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, creating a high probability of stolen base opportunities. **Yordan Alvarez** remains the offensive anchor, carrying an elite xwOBA of .443 into a plus matchup against Johnson. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-focused lineup construction, with **Trea Turner** (75.85) and **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) both positioned at the top of their respective orders to maximize stolen base potential against favorable right-handed starters.\n\nStrategic platoon and situational edges define the remainder of our lineup. **Kazuma Okamoto** (70.30) stands out as a high-floor play, leveraging a significant platoon advantage against the struggling Williamson. Meanwhile, **Christian Yelich** (67.44) and **Hector Rodriguez** (66.09) receive strong bumps due to advantageous matchups against Pallante and Scherzer, respectively. Our most difficult decision was the exclusion of **Carson Benge** (54.74). While he presents solid secondary value, the efficiency gap\u2014particularly regarding platoon splits against the left-handed Herz\u2014pushed him to the bench in favor of higher-projected starters. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given the current late-season schedule. While we are confident in our roster, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (63.94) carries a \"Lineup Pending\" tag; should his status change or the order shift significantly, his efficiency could fluctuate. Additionally, we are monitoring **Junior Caminero** (57.32) closely. Despite a respectable score, he faces Wheeler, an elite arm whose skill level effectively negates the usual platoon advantage. We are proceeding with a full start but will keep **Carson Benge** and **Jacob Gonzalez** ready should any late-inning defensive replacements or unexpected scratches occur.",
